Drop stablehlo/integrations (the C++/Python "builder" convenience API).

It's not needed -- this backend builds StableHLO IR directly via normal MLIR
OpBuilder calls against StablehloOps/ChloOps, same as before. It also
doesn't build cleanly in STABLEHLO_EXTERNAL_PROJECT_BUILD mode (the mode
LLVM_EXTERNAL_PROJECTS puts us in): integrations/cpp/builder's CMakeLists.txt
does `list(GET MLIR_INCLUDE_DIRS 0 mlir_includes)`, but MLIR_INCLUDE_DIRS
(plural) is only ever set by find_package(MLIR CONFIG) in
STABLEHLO_STANDALONE_BUILD mode -- in the external-project mode it's unset,
so the GET resolves to a stale/absent cache entry and the path ends up
literally containing "NOTFOUND".

--- a/stablehlo/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/stablehlo/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -14,7 +14,6 @@
 add_subdirectory(api)
 add_subdirectory(conversions)
 add_subdirectory(dialect)
-add_subdirectory(integrations)
 add_subdirectory(reference)
 add_subdirectory(tests)
 add_subdirectory(testdata)
